  "goodToKnow": "Der Erzieher (die Erzieherin) is a nursery or day-care teacher, working in a Kita or Kindergarten, and the job requires several years of vocational training in Germany. Since 2013, every child from age one has a legal right to a Kita place, but there's a big shortage of Erzieher. Erziehen means to bring up or educate: gut erzogen (well brought up). Die Erziehung is upbringing. The word Kindergarten, which English borrowed, was coined by Friedrich Fröbel in 1840."
